           <groupId>com.graphql-java-kickstart</groupId>
           <artifactId>graphql-spring-boot-starter</artifactId>
           <version>13.0.0</version>
           <scope>provided</scope>
       </dependency>
   </dependencies>
   ```

2. **Create GraphQL Schema**:

   Define your GraphQL schema using SDL (Schema Definition Language) in a `.graphqls` file. Create a file named `schema.graphqls` in the `src/main/resources` directory:

   ```graphql
   type Company {
       id: ID!
       name: String!
       address: String
       contacts: [Contact]
   }

   type Contact {
       id: ID!
       name: String!
       mailId: String!
       companies: [Company]
   }

   type Query {
       getAllCompanies: [Company]
       getCompanyById(id: ID!): Company
       getAllContacts: [Contact]
       getContactById(id: ID!): Contact
   }

   type Mutation {
       createCompany(name: String!, address: String): Company
       updateCompany(id: ID!, name: String!, address: String): Company
       deleteCompany(id: ID!): ID
       createContact(name: String!, mailId: String!): Contact
       updateContact(id: ID!, name: String!, mailId: String!): Contact
       deleteContact(id: ID!): ID
   }
   ```

3. **Create Entity DTOs**:

   Create DTOs (Data Transfer Objects) for `Company` and `Contact` to map the GraphQL input and output:

   ```java
   public class CompanyDTO {
       private String id;
       private String name;
       private String address;
       private List<ContactDTO> contacts;

       // Constructors, getters, setters
   }

   public class ContactDTO {
       private String id;
       private String name;
       private String mailId;
