   ```

5. **Create GraphQL Resolvers**:

   Implement GraphQL resolvers to connect GraphQL queries and mutations to the service methods. You can use libraries like `graphql-java-tools` or create custom resolvers:

   ```java
   @GraphQLComponent
   public class CompanyResolver {
       // Implement resolvers for Company queries and mutations
   }

   @GraphQLComponent
   public class ContactResolver {
       // Implement resolvers for Contact queries and mutations
   }
   ```

6. **Configure GraphQL Endpoint**:

   Configure the GraphQL endpoint in your `application.properties` or `application.yml` file:

   ```properties
   graphql.servlet.mapping=/graphql
   ```

7. **Create GraphQL Controller**:

   Create a GraphQL controller to handle incoming GraphQL requests:

   ```java
   @RestController
   @RequestMapping("/graphql")
   public class GraphQLController {

       @Autowired
       private GraphQL graphQL;

       @PostMapping
       public ResponseEntity<Object> graphql(@RequestBody Map<String, Object> request) {
           ExecutionResult executionResult = graphQL.execute(new ExecutionInput(request));
           return ResponseEntity.ok(executionResult);
       }
