In this example, each method stops the iteration when the element equals `3`, demonstrating how you can break out of an array iteration using different techniques.

Yes, you can use both `style` and `class` attributes on a `div` element. The `style` attribute allows you to apply inline CSS directly to the element, while the `class` attribute assigns the element to one or more CSS classes defined in a stylesheet.

