http-server
```

By default, `http-server` will start serving files on `http://localhost:8080`.

### 5. Open Your Project in a Browser

Open your web browser and go to `http://localhost:8080`. You should see your `index.html` page, and you can check the console for output from your JavaScript files.

### Example:

Here’s a detailed example with your project files:

1. **Directory Structure**:
   ```
   /project-root
   ├── index.html
   ├── DIContainer.js
   ├── Logger.js
   ├── UserService.js
   └── main.js
   ```

2. **index.html**:
   ```html
   <!DOCTYPE html>
   <html lang="en">
   <head>
     <meta charset="UTF-8">
     <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
     <title>Dependency Injection Example</title>
   </head>
   <body>
     <h1>Check the console for output</h1>
     <script type="module" src="main.js"></script>
   </body>
   </html>
   ```

3. **DIContainer.js**:
   ```javascript
   // DIContainer.js
   class DIContainer {
     constructor() {
       this.services = {};
     }

     register(name, dependency) {
       this.services[name] = dependency;
     }

     get(name) {
       return this.services[name];
     }
   }

   export default DIContainer;
   ```

4. **Logger.js**:
   ```javascript
