To ensure that the spans are displayed without overlapping and properly spaced, we can adjust the styles and ensure that each span takes its own line by using `display: block`. Here's how you can modify your JavaScript code:

### JavaScript Code

```javascript
(() => {
    const messages = [
        { type: 'error', text: 'This is an error message' },
        { type: 'warning', text: 'This is a warning message' },
        { type: 'info', text: 'This is an info message' },
        { type: 'success', text: 'This is a success message' }
    ];

    const styles = {
        error: 'color: white; background-color: red; padding: 5px; margin: 20px; border-radius: 3px; display: block;',
