5. **Catch Block**: Catches any errors in the promise chain and updates the promise response accordingly.

This approach maintains the promise chain properly and handles cases where `fetchUserDetailsForEmpCode` is not called by returning a resolved promise.

Certainly! The `MutationObserver` is a powerful feature in JavaScript that allows you to listen for changes to the DOM. Here's an example of how to use it to monitor when a new script element is added or removed from the document:

### Example Code:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>MutationObserver Example</title>
</head>
<body>
    <button id="addScriptButton">Add Script</button>
    <button id="removeLastScriptButton" style="display:none;">Remove Last Script</button>

    <script>
        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
            const customComponentsIdList = [];

            const addScriptButtonEl = document.getElementById('addScriptButton');
            const removeScriptButtonEl = document.getElementById('removeLastScriptButton');

            function addScript() {
                const scriptId = `script-${customComponentsIdList.length + 1}`;
                const script = document.createElement('script');
                script.src = 'path/to/your/script.js'; // Replace with actual script URL
                script.id = scriptId;
                document.body.appendChild(script);
                customComponentsIdList.push(scriptId);
                console.log(`Script with ID ${scriptId} added.`);
                updateButtonVisibility();
            }

            function removeLastScript() {
                const lastScriptId = customComponentsIdList.pop(); // Remove the last script ID from the array
                if (lastScriptId) {
                    const script = document.getElementById(lastScriptId);
                    if (script) {
                        script.parentElement.removeChild(script);
                        console.log(`Script with ID ${lastScriptId} has been removed.`);
                    } else {
                        console.log(`Script with ID ${lastScriptId} does not exist in the DOM.`);
                    }
                } else {
                    console.log('No scripts in customComponentsIdList to remove.');
                }
                updateButtonVisibility();
            }

            function updateButtonVisibility() {
                if (customComponentsIdList.length > 0) {
                    removeScriptButtonEl.style.display = 'inline-block';
                } else {
                    removeScriptButtonEl.style.display = 'none';
                }
            }

            addScriptButtonEl.addEventListener('click', addScript);
            removeScriptButtonEl.addEventListener('click', removeLastScript);

            const observer = new MutationObserver((mutationsList) => {
                for (const mutation of mutationsList) {
                    if (mutation.type === 'childList') {
                        if (mutation.addedNodes.length > 0) {
                            console.log('A child node has been added:', mutation.addedNodes);
                        }
                        if (mutation.removedNodes.length > 0) {
                            console.log('A child node has been removed:', mutation.removedNodes);
                        }
                    }
                }
            });

            observer.observe(document.body, { childList: true });

            updateButtonVisibility();
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:

1. **HTML Structure**:
   - Two buttons are created: "Add Script" and "Remove Last Script".
   - The "Remove Last Script" button is initially hidden.

2. **JavaScript Initialization**:
   - The script waits for the DOM to fully load before executing the code.
   - The `customComponentsIdList` array keeps track of the IDs of added script elements.

3. **Button Event Listeners**:
   - `addScriptButtonEl` adds a new script element to the body and updates the visibility of the "Remove Last Script" button.
   - `removeScriptButtonEl` removes the last added script element and updates the visibility of the "Remove Last Script" button.

4. **MutationObserver**:
   - A `MutationObserver` is created to monitor changes to the body of the document.
   - The observer listens for `childList` mutations, which detect when child nodes are added or removed.
   - When a mutation is detected, the observer logs information about the added or removed nodes.

5. **Observer Configuration**:
   - The observer is configured to watch for changes to the children of the body element (`{ childList: true }`).

6. **Update Button Visibility**:
   - The `updateButtonVisibility` function shows or hides the "Remove Last Script" button based on whether there are any script elements in the `customComponentsIdList`.

This example demonstrates how to dynamically add and remove script elements while using a `MutationObserver` to log changes to the DOM. Replace `'path/to/your/script.js'` with the actual URL of the script you want to add.

