To remove all elements (children) of a specific `div` element, you can use one of the following methods in JavaScript:

### Method 1: Using `innerHTML`
```javascript
const divElement = document.getElementById('yourDivId');
divElement.innerHTML = '';
```
This method sets the `innerHTML` property of the `div` to an empty string, effectively removing all its child elements.

### Method 2: Using `removeChild` in a loop
```javascript
const divElement = document.getElementById('yourDivId');
while (divElement.firstChild) {
    divElement.removeChild(divElement.firstChild);
}
```
This method loops through the children of the `div` and removes each one until no children are left.

### Method 3: Using `replaceChildren`
```javascript
const divElement = document.getElementById('yourDivId');
divElement.replaceChildren();
```
This method removes all child nodes of the `div` element in a more concise way.

### Example:
Here is an example that demonstrates all three methods:

