If you're rendering Markdown content in a Node.js application and want to apply the GitHub Markdown CSS to it, you have a couple of options:

1. **Include the CSS link in your HTML template**: If you're rendering HTML templates using a templating engine like EJS or Pug, you can include the CSS link directly in your template file. Here's an example using EJS:

   ```html
   <!-- layout.ejs -->
   <!DOCTYPE html>
   <html lang="en">
   <head>
     <meta charset="UTF-8">
     <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
     <title>Markdown with GitHub Markdown CSS</title>
