In `react-select`, you can't directly set the `title` attribute on a selected option by default, but you can achieve this by using the `components` prop to create a custom `SingleValue` component. This allows you to add the `title` attribute to the selected option for hover tooltips.

Here’s an example:

```jsx
import React from "react";
import Select from "react-select";

// Custom SingleValue component with title attribute
const CustomSingleValue = ({ children, ...props }) => {
  return (
    <div title={children} {...props.innerProps}>
      {children}
    </div>
  );
};

const options = [
  { value: "kanpur", label: "Delhi via Kanpur from Patna" },
  { value: "lucknow", label: "Delhi via Lucknow from Patna" },
  // other options
];

const ExampleSelect = () => {
  const handleChange = (selectedOption) => {
    console.log(selectedOption);
  };

  return (
    <Select
      options={options}
      onChange={handleChange}
      components={{ SingleValue: CustomSingleValue }}
      placeholder="Select an option"
    />
  );
};

export default ExampleSelect;
```

In this example, the `CustomSingleValue` component adds a `title` attribute to the selected option so that it will show a tooltip with the full label when hovered over.

