```jsx
import React from 'react';
import PropTypes from 'prop-types';
import { FaQuestion } from 'react-icons/fa'; // Import default icon

const IconComponent = ({ iconName }) => {
  // Define a mapping of icon names to corresponding icon components
  const iconMap = {
    // Add more icons here as needed
    'FaHome': () => import('react-icons/fa').then(module => module.FaHome),
    'FaSearch': () => import('react-icons/fa').then(module => module.FaSearch),
    'FaSettings': () => import('react-icons/fa').then(module => module.FaCog),
    'FaUser': () => import('react-icons/fa').then(module => module.FaUser),
    // Add more icons above as needed
  };

  // Check if the requested iconName exists in the iconMap
  const Icon = iconMap[iconName] || (() => FaQuestion); // Default to FaQuestion if not found

  return <Icon />;
};

IconComponent.propTypes = {
  iconName: PropTypes.string.isRequired,
};

export default IconComponent;
```

With this approach, you define a mapping of icon names to corresponding dynamic imports of the required icons. If the requested iconName is found in the mapping, it dynamically imports and returns the corresponding icon component. If the iconName is not found, it defaults to FaQuestion. Adjust the iconMap and import statements according to your specific icon set and needs.

