```java
import java.util.Optional;

public enum Status {
    DRAFTED("Drafted"),
    PUBLISHED("Ongoing"),
    COMPLETED("Completed");

    private final String name;

    Status(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }

    // Modify to return Optional<Status> by name
    public static Optional<Status> fromName(String name) {
        for (Status status : values()) {
            if (status.name.equals(name)) {
                return Optional.of(status);
            }
        }
        return Optional.empty(); // No match found
    }
}
```

With this modification, the `fromName` method returns an `Optional<Status>`. If a matching enum value is found, it returns an `Optional` containing that value; otherwise, it returns an empty `Optional`. This allows you to handle the absence of a matching value without throwing an exception.

